From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 21:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: adaptive context checkpointing -- stop creating
 checkpoints that are always discarded unused (+3.4% score)

`llama-server` creates context checkpoints while evaluating a prompt for any
model whose memory cannot be partially rolled back (SWA, recurrent, hybrid).
Two things are paid for each one:

  * the prompt is deliberately BROKEN at `{4 + n_ubatch, 4}` tokens from its
    end (`checkpoint_offsets`, ref llama.cpp PR 20288) so the state can be
    captured before those tokens are evaluated -- a 528-token prompt therefore
    runs as **three** `llama_decode` calls of 12 + 512 + 4 instead of one;
  * `llama_state_seq_get_data` copies the whole sequence state into a fresh
    `std::vector` on each break.

A checkpoint can only ever be used if a LATER request into the same slot shares
a prefix long enough to reach it (`cur.pos_max <= pos_next`). When it does not,
the next task erases it unused -- the server logs `erased invalidated context
checkpoint` -- and the entire cost was loss. On single-turn or non-overlapping
traffic that is every checkpoint, on every request, forever.

The patch replaces the unconditional `params_base.n_ctx_checkpoints > 0` gate
with a credit that observes what the traffic actually does: creation is allowed
while credit remains, a successful restore refills it to 4, a task that
discards its checkpoints without ever restoring one spends one, and after 64
dry tasks a single probe task is let through so traffic that starts sharing
prefixes turns the feature back on by itself. Multi-turn chat, which restores
checkpoints constantly, never loses them. `LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_CKPT=0` restores
stock behaviour and is the A/B toggle used below.

Nothing about what the model computes changes: a missing checkpoint only ever
means the prompt is re-evaluated from a shorter cached prefix, which is
precisely what stock already does whenever no checkpoint matches.

Measured on the trusted-runner box with a faithful replica of
`Sources/runner/base.ts` (unique prompts per request, so every run is
cache-cold exactly as the ranked harness is), same binary with the env toggle,
**8 arms interleaved off/on/on/off/off/on/on/off**, 9 measured runs each:

| arm | TTFT | prefill tok/s | decode tok/s | minflt / ttft req |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| off | 0.24876 | 4130.7 | 166.05 | 52736 |
| on  | 0.20643 | 4506.7 | 163.78 | 22022 |
| on  | 0.20764 | 4486.7 | 163.51 | 22002 |
| off | 0.24922 | 4104.1 | 166.05 | 52736 |
| off | 0.24956 | 4111.1 | 166.07 | 52736 |
| on  | 0.20949 | 4411.2 | 163.74 | 22022 |
| on  | 0.20912 | 4399.7 | 163.64 | 22002 |
| off | 0.24956 | 4111.1 | 166.07 | 52736 |

Medians: **ttft 0.24922 -> 0.20838 (x1.1960), prefill 4111.1 -> 4448.9
(x1.0822), decode 166.05 -> 163.69 (x0.9858)**. The ttft and prefill arms are
fully disjoint. Modelled score `0.9858^0.65 x 1.0822^0.20 x 1.1960^0.15` =
**+3.39%**, i.e. 1.3872 -> ~1.434.

The decode term is an artefact of how the harness measures decode, and it is
expected: `decode = (t_full(534,128) - t_ttft(534)) / 127`, so any saving that
lands on the ttft request also has to land on the full request or the
subtraction charges the difference to decode. Here ttft falls 40.8 ms and the
full request falls 28 ms, and the 12.8 ms gap is the -1.4%. It is bought back
many times over by the ttft and prefill terms.

Minor faults per ttft request fall 52736 -> 22022 (-30714, about 120 MiB of
first-touch state) and per full request 21167 -> 3439, which is the state-copy
half of the mechanism measured independently of any clock.

Firing is proven structurally from the server log, not from timing
(`llama-server -v`, 8 unique 528-token requests):

```
task  0 | created context checkpoint 1 of 32     chunks: 0, 11, 523
task 11 | created context checkpoint 2 of 32     chunks: 0, 11, 523
task 22 ... task 67                              chunks: 0            <- one decode call
```

Two tasks pay (the credit), every task after that creates zero checkpoints and
evaluates the prompt in a single `llama_decode`.

Correctness:

* **The gate is bit-identical.** Only `libllama-server-impl.so` changes;
  `libggml-hip.so.0`, `libllama.so.0` and the `llama-perplexity` executable are
  untouched by this patch, and the symbol it adds is unreachable from the
  perplexity path. Runner's exact gate command
  (`llama-perplexity -m $MODEL -f corpus -ngl 99 -c 512 --chunks 8`), 3 loads
  per arm in one session: **stock 5.2611 5.2611 5.2611, candidate 5.2611
  5.2611 5.2611** -- 0.000%.
* **The served path is bit-identical too.** 16 varied prompts x 64 greedy
  tokens through `llama-server`, both arms, same binary: **16/16
  byte-identical**, and the sampled-token logprobs agree to
  **max |dlogprob| = 0.000e+00**. Removing the split changes no arithmetic on
  this model -- the batch is simply handed to `llama_context` whole, and it
  splits it into the same 512-wide ubatches.
* Firing verified from the server log (above), not from a clock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
index 4655b518e..663513a47 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -958,6 +958,40 @@ private:
     int slots_debug = 0;
     int n_empty_consecutive = 0;
 
+    // [gainz] adaptive context checkpointing.
+    //
+    // For models whose memory cannot be partially rolled back (SWA, recurrent,
+    // hybrid) the prompt loop creates context checkpoints while evaluating a
+    // prompt.  Each one costs an extra llama_decode call -- the prompt is
+    // deliberately broken at {4 + n_ubatch, 4} tokens from its end purely so the
+    // state can be captured before those tokens are evaluated -- plus a full
+    // llama_state_seq_get_data copy of the sequence state.
+    //
+    // A checkpoint only ever pays for itself if a LATER request into the same
+    // slot shares a prefix long enough to reach it.  When it does not, the next
+    // task erases it unused ("erased invalidated context checkpoint") and the
+    // whole cost was loss.  On single-turn / non-overlapping traffic that is
+    // every checkpoint, on every request, forever.
+    //
+    // The credit below makes it self-tuning instead of unconditional: creation
+    // is allowed while there is credit, a successful restore refills it, a task
+    // that discards checkpoints without restoring one spends it, and after a
+    // long dry spell a single probe task is allowed through so traffic that
+    // starts sharing prefixes turns the feature back on.  Nothing about what the
+    // model computes changes -- a missing checkpoint only ever means the prompt
+    // is re-evaluated, which is exactly what happens today.
+    static constexpr int CKPT_CREDIT_MAX  = 4;
+    static constexpr int CKPT_PROBE_EVERY = 64;
+
+    bool ckpt_adaptive   = [] {
+        const char * e = getenv("LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_CKPT");
+        return e == nullptr || atoi(e) != 0;
+    }();
+    int  ckpt_credit     = 2;
+    int  ckpt_idle       = 0;
+    int  ckpt_wasted     = 0;
+    int  ckpt_last_task  = -1;
+
     std::unique_ptr<server_prompt_cache> prompt_cache;
 
     server_metrics metrics;
@@ -3352,6 +3386,10 @@ private:
                                         // restore the draft's speculative state
                                         common_speculative_set_state(spec.get(), slot.id, it->data_spec);
 
+                                        // [gainz] a restore proves checkpoints are paying off on this traffic
+                                        ckpt_credit = CKPT_CREDIT_MAX;
+                                        ckpt_idle   = 0;
+
                                         pos_next = std::min(pos_next, std::max(it->pos_min + 1, it->pos_max));
                                         n_past   = std::min(slot.prompt.tokens.size_up_to_pos(pos_next), (size_t) it->n_tokens);
                                         SLT_TRC(slot, "restored context checkpoint (pos_min = %d, pos_max = %d, n_tokens = %" PRId64 ", n_past = %d, size = %.3f MiB)\n", it->pos_min, it->pos_max, it->n_tokens, n_past, (float) it->size() / 1024 / 1024);
@@ -3372,6 +3410,8 @@ private:
                                     const auto & cur = *it;
                                     if (cur.pos_max > pos_next) {
                                         SLT_TRC(slot, "erased invalidated context checkpoint (pos_min = %d, pos_max = %d, n_tokens = %" PRId64 ", n_swa = %d, pos_next = %d, size = %.3f MiB)\n", cur.pos_min, cur.pos_max, cur.n_tokens, n_swa, pos_next, (float) cur.size() / 1024 / 1024);
+                                        // [gainz] created, never restored
+                                        ckpt_wasted++;
                                         it = slot.prompt.checkpoints.erase(it);
                                     } else {
                                         ++it;
@@ -3438,6 +3478,29 @@ private:
 
                     bool do_checkpoint = params_base.n_ctx_checkpoints > 0;
 
+                    // [gainz] adaptive context checkpointing -- see ckpt_credit above.
+                    // Settled once per task, before the first chunk of its prompt is
+                    // assembled, so every chunk of one prompt makes the same decision.
+                    if (ckpt_adaptive) {
+                        if (ckpt_last_task != slot.task->id) {
+                            ckpt_last_task = slot.task->id;
+
+                            if (ckpt_wasted > 0) {
+                                ckpt_wasted = 0;
+                                if (ckpt_credit > 0) {
+                                    ckpt_credit--;
+                                }
+                            }
+
+                            if (ckpt_credit == 0 && ++ckpt_idle >= CKPT_PROBE_EVERY) {
+                                ckpt_credit = 1;
+                                ckpt_idle   = 0;
+                            }
+                        }
+
+                        do_checkpoint = do_checkpoint && ckpt_credit > 0;
+                    }
+
                     // make checkpoints only for completion tasks
                     do_checkpoint = do_checkpoint && slot.task->type == SERVER_TASK_TYPE_COMPLETION;
 
